{
  "_doc": "/auto-merge: merge open pull requests unattended. A PR merges only when it carries the opt-in label AND its merge manifest says `merge: auto`, CI is green, it is mergeable, every PR in its `after` list has merged, and /peer-review accepts it. Project-owned and committed; bin/init seeds it once and never overwrites it. A scheduled run reads this file from the trunk, so turning it on or off is a change to the trunk and lands through a PR. Read by .claude/skills/auto-merge/auto-merge.sh.",

